    "lastCommit": {
      "id": "50edd5ae119952360a91f30a95f27bd7a3d4c171",
      "message": "QOL #220 FINAL PHYSICAL LAYOUT CORRECTION \u2014 the effect unit sits beside AC, not below the whole stat block\n\nRoot cause: the developed-glyph effect unit (effectGlyphRow) was a literal\nsibling <View> rendered between statGrid and defs, so any active effect\ninserted a standalone vertical row beneath HP/AC/ATK/DMG and pushed\nWEAK/DEF/RESIST/DEALS/STRIKES downward \u2014 confirmed against the owner's\nphysical Golem screenshot, which showed AC with substantial unused\nhorizontal space to its right instead.\n\nFix: wrapped statGrid and the conditional effectGlyphRow in a shared\nstatRow flex container (flexDirection: row, alignItems: flex-start).\nstatGrid now takes flex:1, so with no effect present the row renders\nbyte-identical to the old layout; with one effect present, the glyph\ncolumn sits beside the stat grid instead of below it. The glyph+status\ncolumn's own height (22dp glyph + two ~9dp status lines) stays within the\nstat grid's natural two-row height, so adding or removing one effect does\nnot change the row's total height \u2014 WEAK/DEALS/STRIKES no longer move.\nMultiple simultaneous effects wrap horizontally within effectGlyphRow,\neach keeping its own magnitude/duration centered underneath, no shared\nlower chip.\n\nAlso enlarged the compact-card glyph 16dp -> 22dp (effectGlyphArt) so it\nreads as a deliberate status emblem at normal viewing distance on device,\nstill well under the 28dp GLYPH_ART_SIZE.combat reference used elsewhere.\nMagnitude/duration text size is unchanged \u2014 only the glyph grew. No change\nto which glyph is selected, the six developed glyph mappings, effect\nmechanics/magnitude/duration, status semantics, expanded-card behavior,\nenemy weapon coating behavior, or knowledge/discovery rules.\n\nAdded testID=\"enemy-stat-row\" / \"enemy-stat-grid\" / \"enemy-defs\" (compact\ncard only) purely for structural test discoverability, matching the\nexisting enemy-effect-glyph-${coatingKind} convention.\n\nRegression: new geometry suite in\nqol220AcAdjacentEffectIndicator.test.tsx, cases A-F (no effect / one acid\neffect / one other effect / multiple effects / expiration / height-position\ncontract), using a hop-count-agnostic ancestor-membership check\n(isDescendantOf) rather than brittle fixed-depth .parent chains, because\nRN's composite-wrapper/host-node pairing for View/Image made naive\n.parent.parent.parent traversal unreliable. Negative control: temporarily\nrestored the old sibling-row structure in production code -> the 5\nstructural cases went RED; reverted -> full 29/29 suite GREEN.\n\nValidation: focused suite 29/29; governed gates (storeceiling, quotedpins,\notastamp, kitexports) green; typecheck:ci clean; typecheck:tests clean at\nbaseline; lint clean; full fast suite 1435/1435 suites, 16636/16639 tests\n(3 pre-existing skips), 0 failures.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LGFtzR6AQJbu4XdR28y3fX",
      "dateCreated": "2026-09-27T18:54:52Z",
